{"id":"feature-store-lookup","t":"Online feature store lookup with TTLs and defaults","tags":["MLOps","Feature Engineering"],"d":"Easy","rt":"python","fn":"lookup","tol":[1e-06,1e-08],"pkgs":[],"st":"Write `lookup(store, entity, features, now, ttl, defaults)` for an online feature store.\n\n- `store[entity][feature]` is a `(value, timestamp)` pair. Entities or features may be missing.\n- `ttl[feature]` is a maximum age in seconds, or `None` for no expiry. Features missing from `ttl` never expire.\n- A stored value is **usable** if `timestamp <= now` (a value from the future is a bug in a backfill and must not leak) and, when a TTL applies, `now - timestamp <= ttl`.\n- Unusable or missing features take `defaults[feature]`, or `None` if there is no default.\n\nReturn `{\"values\": {feature: value}, \"defaulted\": sorted list of features that used the fallback}`.","starter":"def lookup(store, entity, features, now, ttl, defaults):\n    \"\"\"Return {\"values\": ..., \"defaulted\": [...]}\"\"\"\n    row = store.get(entity, {})\n    return {\"values\": {f: row[f][0] for f in features if f in row}, \"defaulted\": []}\n","hints":["Treat \"missing\", \"expired\" and \"from the future\" the same way: fall back to the default.","Use dict.get for both ttl and defaults so absent keys behave as documented."],"sol":"def lookup(store, entity, features, now, ttl, defaults):\n    row = store.get(entity, {})\n    values, defaulted = {}, []\n    for f in features:\n        ok = False\n        if f in row:\n            v, ts = row[f]\n            limit = ttl.get(f)\n            ok = ts <= now and (limit is None or now - ts <= limit)\n        if ok:\n            values[f] = v\n        else:\n            values[f] = defaults.get(f)\n            defaulted.append(f)\n    return {\"values\": values, \"defaulted\": sorted(defaulted)}\n","ex_md":"## Why TTLs\nA seven-day click count that stopped updating a week ago is not a seven-day count any more. Serving it silently gives the model a value from a different distribution than training. A TTL turns staleness into an explicit default the model was trained to expect.\n\n## Why reject future timestamps\nIf a backfill writes values stamped after `now`, serving or training on them leaks future information. Point-in-time correctness is the main reason feature stores exist: training joins and online lookups must both see only values that existed at the decision time.\n\n## Defaults and monitoring\nLog the defaulted list. A spike in defaults is often the first sign that an upstream pipeline broke, well before model metrics move.\n\n## Interview follow-ups\n- How do you make the training-time join use the same TTL rules as serving?","nex":2,"shown":[{"in":"{'u1': {'clicks_7d': (12, 1000), 'avg_order': (35.5, 400), 'country': ('DE', 10), 'score': (0.8, 2000)}, 'u2': {'clicks_7d': (3, 990)}}\n'u1'\n['clicks_7d', 'avg_order', 'country']\n1100\n{'clicks_7d': 600, 'avg_order': 300, 'score': 60}\n{'clicks_7d': 0, 'avg_order': 20.0}","out":"{'values': {'clicks_7d': 12, 'avg_order': 20.0, 'country': 'DE'}, 'defaulted': ['avg_order']}"},{"in":"{'u1': {'clicks_7d': (12, 1000), 'avg_order': (35.5, 400), 'country': ('DE', 10), 'score': (0.8, 2000)}, 'u2': {'clicks_7d': (3, 990)}}\n'u1'\n['score', 'clicks_7d']\n1500\n{'clicks_7d': 600, 'avg_order': 300, 'score': 60}\n{'clicks_7d': 0, 'avg_order': 20.0}","out":"{'values': {'score': None, 'clicks_7d': 12}, 'defaulted': ['score']}"}],"lessons":[],"related":[],"theory":[],"ntests":6,"tj":"[{\"a\": [{\"__dict__\": [[\"u1\", {\"__dict__\": [[\"clicks_7d\", {\"__tup__\": [12, 1000]}], [\"avg_order\", {\"__tup__\": [35.5, 400]}], [\"country\", {\"__tup__\": [\"DE\", 10]}], [\"score\", {\"__tup__\": [0.8, 2000]}]]}], [\"u2\", {\"__dict__\": [[\"clicks_7d\", {\"__tup__\": [3, 990]}]]}]]}, \"u1\", [\"clicks_7d\", \"avg_order\", \"country\"], 1100, {\"__dict__\": [[\"clicks_7d\", 600], [\"avg_order\", 300], [\"score\", 60]]}, {\"__dict__\": [[\"clicks_7d\", 0], [\"avg_order\", 20.0]]}], \"e\": {\"__dict__\": [[\"values\", {\"__dict__\": [[\"clicks_7d\", 12], [\"avg_order\", 20.0], [\"country\", \"DE\"]]}], [\"defaulted\", [\"avg_order\"]]]}}, {\"a\": [{\"__dict__\": [[\"u1\", {\"__dict__\": [[\"clicks_7d\", {\"__tup__\": [12, 1000]}], [\"avg_order\", {\"__tup__\": [35.5, 400]}], [\"country\", {\"__tup__\": [\"DE\", 10]}], [\"score\", {\"__tup__\": [0.8, 2000]}]]}], [\"u2\", {\"__dict__\": [[\"clicks_7d\", {\"__tup__\": [3, 990]}]]}]]}, \"u1\", [\"score\", \"clicks_7d\"], 1500, {\"__dict__\": [[\"clicks_7d\", 600], [\"avg_order\", 300], [\"score\", 60]]}, {\"__dict__\": [[\"clicks_7d\", 0], [\"avg_order\", 20.0]]}], \"e\": {\"__dict__\": [[\"values\", {\"__dict__\": [[\"score\", null], [\"clicks_7d\", 12]]}], [\"defaulted\", [\"score\"]]]}}, {\"a\": [{\"__dict__\": [[\"u1\", {\"__dict__\": [[\"clicks_7d\", {\"__tup__\": [12, 1000]}], [\"avg_order\", {\"__tup__\": [35.5, 400]}], [\"country\", {\"__tup__\": [\"DE\", 10]}], [\"score\", {\"__tup__\": [0.8, 2000]}]]}], [\"u2\", {\"__dict__\": [[\"clicks_7d\", {\"__tup__\": [3, 990]}]]}]]}, \"u3\", [\"clicks_7d\", \"country\"], 1000, {\"__dict__\": [[\"clicks_7d\", 600], [\"avg_order\", 300], [\"score\", 60]]}, {\"__dict__\": [[\"clicks_7d\", 0], [\"avg_order\", 20.0]]}], \"e\": {\"__dict__\": [[\"values\", {\"__dict__\": [[\"clicks_7d\", 0], [\"country\", null]]}], [\"defaulted\", [\"clicks_7d\", \"country\"]]]}}, {\"a\": [{\"__dict__\": [[\"u1\", {\"__dict__\": [[\"clicks_7d\", {\"__tup__\": [12, 1000]}], [\"avg_order\", {\"__tup__\": [35.5, 400]}], [\"country\", {\"__tup__\": [\"DE\", 10]}], [\"score\", {\"__tup__\": [0.8, 2000]}]]}], [\"u2\", {\"__dict__\": [[\"clicks_7d\", {\"__tup__\": [3, 990]}]]}]]}, \"u2\", [\"clicks_7d\"], 1590, {\"__dict__\": [[\"clicks_7d\", 600], [\"avg_order\", 300], [\"score\", 60]]}, {\"__dict__\": [[\"clicks_7d\", 0], [\"avg_order\", 20.0]]}], \"e\": {\"__dict__\": [[\"values\", {\"__dict__\": [[\"clicks_7d\", 3]]}], [\"defaulted\", []]]}}, {\"a\": [{\"__dict__\": [[\"u1